        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c9f6dadf-28fa-58fd-9e3a-28d0e7b19bde",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Luca Cordero di Montezemolo, Enzo Ferrari, Piero Ferrari, Jean Todt, Amedeo Felisa, Massimo Fumarola\n- Companies: Ferrari, Fiat S.p.A., Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV\n- Organizations: Confindustria, FIEG, Pininfarina, FerrariWorld\n- Products: Ferrari Ascari, Supercar Challenge, Bugatti Veyron, Aston Martin DBR9\n- Places: Turin, Netherlands, Nürburgring, Silverstone Circuit\n- Topics: automotive industry, corporate merger, video game content, competition judges\n\nFacts:\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo was born on 31 August 1947 and is an Italian businessman.\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo served as Chairman of Ferrari and formerly served as Chairman of Fiat S.p.A. and President of Confindustria and FIEG.\n- Fiat S.p.A., short for Fabbrica Italiana Automobili Torino, was an Italian holding company whose original and core activities were in the automotive industry.\n- On 29 January 2014, Fiat S.p.A. announced that it would merge into the new Netherlands-based holding company Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV before the end of 2014.\n- Fiat S.p.A. was succeeded by Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV.\n- In the Ferrari Ascari competition, the judges included Luca Cordero di Montezemolo, Piero Ferrari, Jean Todt, Amedeo Felisa, Massimo Fumarola, Pininfarina, and more than 22,000 users of FerrariWorld's online website.\n- Piero Ferrari was identified as the second and only living son of Enzo Ferrari.\n- Supercar Challenge includes more than 40 cars, including Ferraris, the Bugatti Veyron, and the Aston Martin DBR9, and it includes 22 tracks including the Nürburgring Grand Prix section and the Silverstone Circuit.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
